WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.879
Every day-two request has to answer
three questions before anything changes:

2
00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:08.500
where does it go, who may say
yes, and what proves it happened.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.244
The book answers them with
platforms the agency already runs:

4
00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.740
the service management platform routes,

5
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.438
the identity governance tool approves,
and Entra ID is where the change lands.

6
00:00:19.438 --> 00:00:23.582
Underneath sits a contract, not a
product: every task has an owner,

7
00:00:23.582 --> 00:00:26.084
every change has an approval on record,

8
00:00:26.084 --> 00:00:31.088
automation runs under a narrow identity,
and evidence comes out the other end.

9
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:34.687
The five rules along the
bottom apply to every request.

10
00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:39.201
If any one is missing, the change may
be right, but it can't be attested.

11
00:00:39.201 --> 00:00:41.350
Module 1 starts at the front door.
